these standards  and often you elect the right  interfaces for your device make sure to  always  carry a bunch of adapters in order to be  able to connect all kinds of different  beamers and monitors  even if the technology is rather  outdated next little thing is a  presenter so something like  this this is also something i always  have in my bag it's a nice and easy  device you can plug it into every pc  and then you don't have to do this  little thing of you know somebody maybe  clicking  advancing the slides on the pc and then  someone else  presenting something and then this is  not really in sync maybe then someone is  already advancing to the next slide  where the presenter still wanted to talk  about the last slide  ah this is always very cumbersome it's  so great if you just always carry  presenter  plug it in the device give the presenter  to your partner to your project lead  whoever is  presenting and again this will make you  look as quite organized quite well  organized if you always carry these  things  have them with you and then at the right  moment in time you can just drag them  out plug them in and it just all  works next is to always carry with you  some additional spare audio conferencing  devices so as a consultant i was always  carrying with me a set of two  little audio spiders so these  combination devices where you have both  a microphone and a speaker  because with these you can easily plug  them into your pc  and then two of them you can often  combine them sync them  and then with two of them even in a  larger meeting room this usually always  gave you enough flexibility  to provide full audio and microphone  coverage  of a larger meeting room so here there  are different brands offering solutions  like that  i actually very frequently use the jabra  devices which i also own myself i will  link now in the video description some  links to these devices that i personally  use  so if you're interested in that just  check them out i also want to share some  points of advice on  online meetings online video meetings  because of course i very well understand  that many of these physical meetings are  not taking place at the moment  and here maybe some obvious things of  course make sure that you're sitting in  an area where you have stable internet  connection  and of course also not too much noise  surrounding you and this might sound  obvious but i still  very very vividly remember the  conversation of two partners and one of  my prior employers  where it was not discussed well the  senior consultant should be promoted  to project lead and one partner made a  very hard case against that  because this partner had an experience  with this consultant  but this consultant was conducting a  probably rather important client  conversation  from a train he was in an audio  conference from a train  due to the of course bad telephone  connection in trains he was dropping in  and off of the call all the time  and this partner was making the point  that apparently this consultant is not  taking his runs abilities seriously  enough  that this consultant should have made  sure that when he is on an important  client call  that he is not sitting in a train that  he is making sure that he has good  connection that he can conduct these  calls  in a professional manner as the client  will expect this consultant to so  frankly when i heard that i thought that  this was quite tough that only for one  incident like that  your promotion is questioned but  apparently obviously some people  things like that to some people this is  extremely important so make sure  you have these things in mind as well to  just not endanger your next promotion to  not endanger your career's way  another point on online video  conferences is of course the proper  technical setup  most people nowadays have laptops where  there is an integrated microphone and an  integrated camera  in most video conferences are just  conducted by sitting in front of a  laptop  using exactly these devices and i trust  this will be the case for most  regular interactions most regular  conferences but especially if you're  having some very important meetings with  very senior people  consider whether you don't want to  upgrade your equipment a bit  and you know in my current role i had  the pleasure to in the last month's  interview lots of people lots of  candidates and you would be surprised  how many of these people  were sitting in dark environments you  could barely properly see them due to  the low quality camera that they used in  the laptop  maybe there were also noise  interferences their audio was not very  clear  of course this will not help you to make  a great impression so think about that  don't you have one two three hundred  euro to spare  to invest in a proper microphone in some  basic lights  maybe even an external camera to  properly make sure that you have a nice  picture  with a couple of hundred bucks you will  be able to significantly improve your  video conferencing setup  and this might be very much worth the  investment especially for facing these  types of situations that are now  highlighted  now in one effort to combine all of  these points i think that there's one  common denominator that really will  define whether you are able to prepare  yourself in the right way or not  because the truth is even if you're 10  minutes early 10 minutes in the room  before the meeting starts  this will usually barely be enough to  connect all your devices to the other  devices  this will be barely enough preparation  time to make sure everything is set up  and works properly  but as soon as you have one little  problem as soon as one thing does not  work as expected  usually you will run out of time and you  will not be able to start the meeting on  time from my experience especially for  important meetings where you want to  make sure that  everything works smoothly you should be  in the meeting room at least 30 minutes  before the meeting start  to make sure and to give you enough time  to set everything up and to have this  fallback option that if  something is not working properly that  you at least have a chance  to find maybe a replacement device to  maybe get an additional microphone from  somewhere  to potentially call a technical support  person that often many client  organizations have  if you are not in the room 30 minutes  before the meetings start you will not  be able  to do this on time so as with most other  things in life as well  good preparation is key be sure that you  behave as a professional especially if  you're working in professional services  and a big part of that certainly is  to make sure that you prepare for your  important meetings in a very meticulous  and diligent way  and of course i do hope that this video  contained a couple of tips which will  help you to do exactly that  but now i would love to hear from you do  you have even more advice on this topic  to share that might be beneficial to  other members of the firm learning  community as well  i would very much appreciate to see  comments from you and of course as you  know every comment also helps with the  youtube algorithm so if you took any  value out of this video at all  please hit the like button for the  youtube algorithm and also subscribe to  the channel  to stay up to date on all my content i'm  releasing new videos every single  saturday here on my channel  if you want to see even more from me i'm  also present on other channels such as  instagram ticktalk or twitch and i also  have a mailing list  you'll find the links to all these  medias below in the video description  and if you would like to learn more  about how to create presentations in the  style of leading consulting firms i once  created a fully fledged online course  exactly on the topic  again link to that in the video  description as well i also want to say  thank you to all the members of firm  learning  you're really making a great  contribution to the channel this is much  appreciated  and if you want to join as well just hit  the join button next to the subscribe  button so if you want to continue your  learning journey with this channel there  will be no videos appearing next to me  so feel free to check them out again i  release videos every single saturday so  see you again next week  until then good weekend to all of you  this is jaime from from learning  bye bye


